## Normalized conditions and compatibility

The machine manifest includes the exact generated graph and revisions;
PacketFlowBridge and five-part HEV/lwIP pin set; MTU, requested/effective buffer,
batching, HEV stack/TCP/UDP-copy/session, memory, notice, and no-fork conditions;
the selected libssh2/OpenSSL adapter and pins; primary/fallback algorithms;
window/buffer/rekey/lifecycle values; mandatory capabilities; license,
maintenance, advisory, rebase, and revalidation obligations; rejected/deferred
states; and eight stable compatibility rows against `m1-runtime-contract/1`.

`TASK-260715-3ejhyy` receives this exact JSON as a precondition and must consume
it as the sole M0 binding source. Its future production factory entry point must
validate before constructing concrete SSH, PacketFlowBridge, or HEV dependencies
and before `NetworkSettingsApplier.apply`.

## Fail-closed and negative evidence

The production CLI validator rejects:

- changed upstream bytes, missing resources, malformed/unreadable manifest;
- reopened tasks, undeclared resources, and explicit supersession;
- unknown fields/schema, any set other than all three M0 inputs, and a stored
  permit inconsistent with recomputation;
- negative/missing/duplicate compatibility rows;
- generated provider graph, HEV pin, libssh2 pin, or OpenSSL pin drift.

The named narrowing test removes one of three M0 inputs and still requires exit
1/permission false. The changed-resource test modifies accepted bytes without
changing the old digest and requires exit 1, proving an upstream replacement
cannot silently retain permission. Absence and malformed read have distinct
stable failure rows.

